# Cursor Rules - FlyRank Frontend AI Engineering

- Follow TypeScript strict mode for all frontend and utility code.
- Always use Conventional Commits 1.0.0 for commit messages.
- Prefer functional React components with explicit props typing.
- Use Tailwind CSS or modular CSS aligned with modern UX best practices.
- Avoid introducing unvalidated mock dependencies or unfinished placeholder blocks.
- Ensure all interactive elements have semantic HTML tags and accessibility attributes.

## Form & Mutation Rules (FE-02)
- Forms must use schema validators with `.trim()` and RFC 5322 regex for emails.
- All form controls require WCAG 2.1 AA a11y: `<label htmlFor>`, `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, and `role="alert"`.
- Form submissions must lock `isSubmitting` and disable trigger buttons to avoid duplicate mutations.
